[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5231804973","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122230#issuecomment-5231804973","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122230","id":5231804973,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABN9cCLQ","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-09T13:37:49Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T13:38:48Z","body":"> I would suggest to instead warn on `free()` calls on yourself.\r\n\r\nHow would you do this without a (probably expensive) callstack check? I think the `_notifying` flag already covers the common cases, as most user code is in `_ready`, `_process`, `_physics_process` etc. Maybe the check can be extended to other such flags? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5231804973/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5231808461","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122230#issuecomment-5231808461","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122230","id":5231808461,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABN9cPzQ","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-09T13:38:42Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T13:38:42Z","body":"I would do this on a `GDScript` source level, not at a core level.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5231808461/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5231822940","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122230#issuecomment-5231822940","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122230","id":5231822940,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABN9dIXA","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-09T13:42:06Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T13:42:06Z","body":"> I would do this on a `GDScript` source level, not at a core level.\r\n\r\nThe problem is that this can also happen in GDExtension. (I didn't check C#).\r\n\r\nMaybe the current approach could already serve as a solution until a fix with more coverage is found? Personally I don't have much knowledge of GDScript machinery, so I don't feel confident making a PR in that area. But I believe this approach can already detect a lot of potential user errors at very little cost (this PR is +14 LoC and an `unlikely` branch outside a hot path).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5231822940/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5232066925","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122230#issuecomment-5232066925","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122230","id":5232066925,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABN9sBbQ","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-09T14:38:15Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T14:38:38Z","body":"> > I would do this on a `GDScript` source level, not at a core level.\r\n> \r\n> The problem is that this can also happen in GDExtension. (I didn't check C#).\r\n\r\nSure, but this is a language level issue. No language allows destructing the object that's running a method, and i'm pretty sure all compilers will complain about it.\r\nThe main difference is probably that a c++ `free()` call does not inform the compiler that it will lead to an Object free, but maybe that's something that can be fixed with annotations.\r\n\r\nI maintain the position that this is not something that should be solved at runtime, simply because it's so fundamental that I consider it more of a language problem than a library problem.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5232066925/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5232140992","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122230#issuecomment-5232140992","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122230","id":5232140992,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABN9wiwA","user":{"login":"NoctemCat","id":22471296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDcxMjk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22471296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat","html_url":"https://github.com/NoctemCat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-09T14:55:53Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T15:13:28Z","body":"> No language allows destructing the object that's running a method\r\n\r\nThe fully valid `delete this;` in C++ enters chat.\r\n\r\nOk, now for actual ideas, maybe we can use the same thing `OBJ_DEBUG_LOCK` is using to prevent the Object from being freed inside the `notification` ? Well the error could be more descriptive I guess and it will only be present in the debug build.\r\n```c++\r\nif (_lock_index.get() > 1) {\r\n\tr_error.argument = 0;\r\n\tr_error.error = Callable::CallError::CALL_ERROR_INVALID_METHOD;\r\n\tERR_FAIL_V_MSG(Variant(), \"Object is locked and can't be freed.\");\r\n}\r\n```\r\nAlso I think I read too much messages about people using `free` on itself during debug, so could this change be breaking even if the previous behaviour was use-after-free and will crash in release?\r\n\r\nEdit: Also it's kind of strange that if you call any method from the notification you can't free itself inside that method, but can inside the notification itself.\r\n<img width=\"838\" height=\"490\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/12003003-5618-4dca-92ac-f7da5f097a0c\" />\r\n\r\nBut I guess it will do nothing for GDExtensions...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5232140992/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5232552930","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122230#issuecomment-5232552930","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122230","id":5232552930,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABN-Jr4g","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-09T16:30:27Z","updated_at":"2026-08-09T16:30:35Z","body":"> The fully valid `delete this;` in C++ enters chat.\r\n\r\nWell, it's valid at a source level (though I would expect compilers to complain practically), but C++ will also crash if you `delete this` and then use-after-free. It doesn't protect you from your own mistakes in the way this PR would introduce.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5232552930/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]